<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="080" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rule set and rate card scope schema: core lookups, scope options, all-BU flag, BU N:N, rate card scope and backfill, scope-column field security, Secure business-unit snapshot column</title>
    <phase>3 Rules (WP3) — rule-set scope (D-171, D-172, D-141), wave W3-6</phase>
    <gate>owner approved the 080 schema for dev 2026-10-20 (D-144), on condition that ontology-r1 reviews it first: the real run waits for ontology-r1's PASS on the script and the -WhatIf output</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New idempotent schema script on dev (additive columns, options, one N:N, one new column on the three core tables) plus a data backfill and field security on two existing columns; no BFF code. The backfill writes rows and S7 changes existing columns, so the run is owner-gated.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Every item, name and value is fixed by the design note section 2; the scripts it copies already exist in scripts/ebilling/ and scripts/.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Live dev schema change on tables other tasks and projects read (sprk_ruleset, sprk_ratecard, sprk_matter, sprk_project, sprk_workassignment), gated by an owner approval and coordinated with ontology-r1 and uac-r2.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>019, 017, 029</deps>
    <tags>dataverse, schema, coordination, security</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-7 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Write scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingRuleSetScopeSchema.ps1, which adds items S1-S4 and S6-S8 of notes/rule-set-scope-design.md section 2 to dev (core-record lookups on sprk_ruleset with RemoveLink, the Record and FirmRecord scope options, the all-business-units flag, the sprk_ruleset-businessunit N:N, a new explicit scope on sprk_ratecard with a one-time backfill, field security on the rule set's scope columns, and the field-secured Secure business-unit snapshot column on the three core tables) plus the sprk_createdbyperson column on sprk_ruleset, sprk_ratecard and sprk_ratecardrate (S9, created by the owning schema), and update the data-model docs. Show the final script and its -WhatIf output to the owner and run it only after the owner approves. S5 (role row) is NOT in this script, nor are the S9 list entries (RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1, which only secures and verifies the column): tasks 081 and 086 ship them with the code the shared guards tie them to.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Dataverse metadata Web API, field security profiles, idempotent schema scripts on EbillingSchema.psm1, and coordinating changes with the projects that read the same tables.</role>

  <goal>After owner approval, dev has every S1-S4 and S6-S8 item and sprk_createdbyperson on the three billing tables (S9, owning-schema part) with the stated names, types, values, delete behaviour and field security; every existing sprk_ratecard row has a scope set by the backfill rule, or is listed as not set; a second run writes nothing; the data-model docs describe the new columns, the fail-closed rule and the snapshot's read rule; ontology-r1 and uac-r2 had a notice before and after the run.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design: projects/ebilling-r1/notes/rule-set-scope-design.md sections 2, 3.5, 4.5, 5.2 and 12 (uac-r2 review). Decisions: D-136 / ontology D-171 (levels, BU filter), D-137 / ontology D-172 (direct inheritance; no delete-Restrict; explicit scope on rule sets AND rate cards; GitHub #2129, #2132, DEF-027), D-138, D-141 (Q1: the Secure business-unit snapshot is ebilling's column, read only while Secure; Proposal A, an always-maintained home-BU lookup, is rejected). sprk_ruleset today: sprk_scope local choice ClientDefault 100000000, Firm 100000001; sprk_firm RemoveLink (docs/data-model/sprk_ruleset.md:29-30). sprk_ratecard today: optional sprk_matter / sprk_project / sprk_workassignment lookups, RemoveLink on dev, no scope column (docs/data-model/sprk_ratecard.md:17-20); RateCardResolver derives the scope from the lookups (RateCardResolver.cs:133-142). The field-security pattern to copy: scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 Ensure-Profile (:324-336), a reader profile on every business unit default team plus a writer profile for the BFF application user only.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingRuleSetScopeSchema.ps1</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/data-model/sprk_ruleset.md</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/data-model/sprk_ratecard.md</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/data-model/sprk_matter-related-tables.md and docs/data-model/sprk_workassignment.md (S8 column; the project's columns are documented where sprk_project's are today)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/EbillingSchema.psm1 (Add-Lookup :334, Add-LocalChoice :467, Add-ManyToMany :777; module default delete RemoveLink :337)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingTimekeeperRateCardSchema.ps1:431-436 (the three core lookups to copy)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingApprovalSchema.ps1:168 (N:N precedent)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingSubmissionIntegrityOption.ps1 (insert an option, refuse relabel or renumber)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingPolicyStoreSchema.ps1 (two-option column with a default)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 (Ensure-Profile :324-336: reader / writer field security profiles)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="019" status="completed">sprk_ruleset table and sprk_scope choice</dependency>
      <dependency task="017" status="completed">sprk_ratecard table and its core lookups</dependency>
      <dependency task="029" status="completed">WP1 schema in dev and SpaarkeMaster</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-137 / ontology D-172 (#2132)">No delete-Restrict anywhere in this script. The three sprk_ruleset core lookups (S1) use RemoveLink, the module default; the three sprk_ratecard core lookups are not touched. Quote in the script header: "Deleting a matter must never require first deleting its rate cards or rule sets, because the user may lack permission."</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S1">sprk_ruleset.sprk_matter → sprk_matter, sprk_project → sprk_project, sprk_workassignment → sprk_workassignment; relationships sprk_matter_ruleset_matter, sprk_project_ruleset_project, sprk_workassignment_ruleset_workassignment; optional.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S2, D-172">Insert sprk_ruleset.sprk_scope options Record = 100000002 and FirmRecord = 100000003. ClientDefault 100000000 and Firm 100000001 are unchanged. If either value or label exists with another meaning, refuse (copy Deploy-EbillingSubmissionIntegrityOption.ps1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S3">sprk_ruleset.sprk_allbusinessunits: two-option, display "All business units", default Yes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S4 (Q2, approved with the script)">N:N sprk_ruleset_businessunit between sprk_ruleset and businessunit. Pre-check EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='businessunit')?$select=CanBeInManyToMany: if false, STOP (escalation), do not create a fallback table.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note S6, D-172, D-147 / ontology D-174, DEF-027">sprk_ratecard.sprk_scope: new local choice, display "Applies to", Firm = 100000000, CoreRecord = 100000001, optional, no default. Backfill only rows whose sprk_scope is empty: exactly one core lookup → CoreRecord; none → Firm; two or more → leave empty and list. Never overwrite a set value. The output lists every card marked Firm (name, id, firm) for the owner. Before marking a card Firm, read its audit history (when auditing is on for sprk_ratecard): if a core lookup (sprk_matter / sprk_project / sprk_workassignment) was ever set and later cleared, mark the card CoreRecord (so it applies to nothing; ontology-r1 condition, D-172 round 3) and list it separately as an orphaned card. If auditing is off, say so in the notes. On spaarkedev1 the Firm list is recorded in notes/080-ruleset-scope-schema.md and confirmed by 085 step 0, not by the owner (D-147 / ontology D-174: dev is test data). In any customer environment the Firm list goes to the owner before 085 is deployed there. The orphan rule above applies in every environment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 8, design note S7">Field-secure sprk_ruleset.sprk_scope, sprk_firm, sprk_matter, sprk_project and sprk_workassignment (IsSecured true), because a model-driven edit of them bypasses the Q9 lock (409 ruleset.scope_locked is the BFF's). Copy the reader / writer profile pair of scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1: Read for every user (reader profile on every business unit's default team), Create / Update for the BFF application user only. Whether the columns join uac-r2's existing pair or an ebilling pair is settled with uac-r2 in the before-notice (step 3). Before securing, list every reader of sprk_scope and sprk_firm (design note section 6 reader table, plus a Grep of src/ and src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster for both names) and record it. The read-only form controls are 079's (SpaarkeMaster), not this script's.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-141 (Q1), design note S8, uac-r2 conditions b and c">New column sprk_securedfrombusinessunit ("Business unit before Secure"), a lookup to businessunit, on sprk_matter, sprk_project and sprk_workassignment; delete behaviour RemoveLink; optional; IsSecured true with a writer profile for the BFF application user only and NO reader profile (no user reads or writes it); on no form and in no view (079 adds none). The column is ebilling's (owner correction: uac-r2 does not build it); its writer is task 087 and its reader task 082. Do NOT add any other business-unit column to the core tables (Proposal A, an always-maintained home-BU lookup, is rejected by D-141).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-141, uac-r2 review item 1, round 2 items 081.3 / 086.3 (a9371df5c1)">S9 split: the owning schema CREATES the column. This script creates sprk_createdbyperson (lookup to systemuser, RemoveLink, created unsecured; shape copied from task 013) on sprk_ruleset, sprk_ratecard and sprk_ratecardrate, the three billing tables ebilling owns. ontology-r1 creates it on sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion. scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 never creates it for these tables ($SolutionHomes): it only secures and verifies it, and its list, like S5 (config/secure-record-owner-role.json), is pinned against BFF code by ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchemaAgreementTests, SecureFamilyConsistencyTests and the census, so tasks 081 (rule set, policy, version) and 086 (rate card, rate) add those list entries in one change with that code. The three core tables gain only S8.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-144, project CLAUDE.md section 5, root CLAUDE.md section 6">The owner approved the 080 schema for dev on 2026-10-20 (D-144), on condition that ontology-r1 reviews it first. Before the real run, ontology-r1 must PASS the final script and the -WhatIf output against existing schema practice (naming, option sets, lookups, ownership, field security, solution placement) and the ontology model. Its findings are fixed and re-checked. The main session asks the owner again if the -WhatIf shows anything the design note does not (a collision, a new item, a change of type or value), or if the review changes the design. Dev only. -WhatIf first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md section 3 (pipeline)">Do NOT edit src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/** (079 syncs it). No forms or views here (079). No plugins, business rules or calculated columns (ADR-002). No file under src/ changes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/rule-set-scope-design.md (sections 2, 3.5, 4.5, 5.2, 12)</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/data.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Ebilling schema script" location="scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingTimekeeperRateCardSchema.ps1">Initialize-EbillingSchema, check-then-create per item, -WhatIf, a tally at the end, publish.</pattern>
      <pattern name="BFF-only column with field security" location="scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1:324-336">Ensure-Profile reader / writer pair; -Verify mode.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Collision check on dev: sprk_ruleset (sprk_matter, sprk_project, sprk_workassignment, sprk_allbusinessunits, sprk_scope option values 100000002-100000003, IsSecured on sprk_scope and sprk_firm), sprk_ratecard.sprk_scope, sprk_securedfrombusinessunit on the three core tables, relationship and intersect names, businessunit CanBeInManyToMany. Record the results in notes/080-ruleset-scope-schema.md.</step>
    <step order="2">List every reader of sprk_ruleset.sprk_scope and sprk_firm (code, views, forms, flows found by Grep and by a dev read of savedquery / systemform fetchxml naming them); record which run as a user without the reader profile.</step>
    <step order="3">Write the script on EbillingSchema.psm1, copying the reference scripts named in relevant-files. S1, S2, S3, S4, S6 column, S7 field security, S8 column and its writer profile, then the S6 backfill (a separate section with its own -WhatIf output and its list of cards marked Firm, CoreRecord and left empty).</step>
    <step order="4">Notice before: post the planned item list, the step 2 reader list and the -WhatIf output to ontology-r1 and uac-r2 (a comment on #2129 and a message to each session); settle with uac-r2 which field security profiles S7 and S8 use. Record the date and the answer.</step>
    <step order="5">ontology-r1 schema review (D-144): send ontology-r1 the final script, the -WhatIf output (including the backfill list) and the design note section 2. Ask it to check the script against existing schema practice and the ontology model. Fix its findings and get its PASS. Record the owner approval (D-144, 2026-10-20) and the PASS, with dates, in the task notes. Go back to the owner only on the conditions of the D-144 constraint.</step>
    <step order="6">Run for real, then run again: the second run reports no created item and writes no row.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify by metadata read: every column, option value, the N:N, the RemoveLink delete behaviour on the three new sprk_ruleset relationships and on the three sprk_securedfrombusinessunit relationships, IsSecured on the five S7 columns and on S8, and the profiles' permissions. Verify by data read: no sprk_ratecard row whose scope was set before the run changed; no core record has sprk_securedfrombusinessunit set (the writer is 087).</step>
    <step order="8">Notice after: send the run result and the backfill list to ontology-r1 and uac-r2.</step>
    <step order="9">Update docs/data-model/sprk_ruleset.md (S1-S4, S7, the four scope values, "a Record / FirmRecord set whose lookup is cleared applies to nothing", "the scope columns are written only by the BFF"), sprk_ratecard.md (S6, the backfill rule, RemoveLink kept, "an empty scope or a CoreRecord card with no lookup is never used"), and the core-table docs (S8: written only on entry to Secure by ProvisionProjectEndpoint or by the path that creates a record into isolation; read only while the record is held in the Secure Record business unit; Unsecure never reads it; excluded from membership discovery).</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="11">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/080-ruleset-scope-schema.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ontology-r1 has not passed the schema review (D-144), or the -WhatIf shows anything the design note does not, STOP before step 6. Do not run anything except -WhatIf.</trigger>
    <trigger>If businessunit reports CanBeInManyToMany = false, STOP and ask the owner to approve option (b) of the design note (an intersect table) as a script change; do not create it on your own.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any planned name or option value exists with another meaning, STOP and present both to the owner; do not rename or renumber.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the backfill finds a card with two or more core lookups, list it and leave it empty; do not choose one.</trigger>
    <trigger>If step 2 finds a reader of sprk_scope or sprk_firm that runs as a user who would not hold the reader profile, STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required before securing the columns: securing them would turn that reader's value into null.</trigger>
    <trigger>If uac-r2 does not agree the S7 / S8 profile choice in step 4, STOP before step 6; do not create a profile that adds members to uac-r2's profiles without their agreement.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a business-unit column other than sprk_securedfrombusinessunit is proposed for the core tables (for example by a review), STOP: D-141 rejects it; raise it to the main session.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>sprk_ruleset.sprk_scope (019) and sprk_ratecard's optional core lookups (017) exist; grep of scripts/ebilling and docs/data-model finds no core lookup on sprk_ruleset, no business-unit link and no rate card scope column. The only business-unit column on the core tables is the system owningbusinessunit, which the secure re-own overwrites (RecordOwnershipResolver.cs:86-87, :2181); UnsecureProjectRequest reassigns to a user, not to a stored business unit.</existing>
    <extension>The existing choice gains two options instead of a new column; the rate card gets the same explicit-scope idea the rule set already has. The BU list needs a relationship, because no existing column can hold a set of business units with referential integrity. S7 changes only the security of existing and S1 columns. S8 cannot extend owningbusinessunit (a system column the re-own rewrites); deriving the business unit from the creator or parent fails when the owner has moved, and the always-maintained alternative is rejected by D-141.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A rule set cannot name a matter, project or work assignment (D-171); a rate card whose record is deleted keeps applying firm-wide (#2132, DEF-027); a model-driven edit can change a Published set's scope behind the Q9 lock; and a business-unit-restricted rule set never applies to a Secure record's invoices (interim B forever).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">Schema script</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">Metadata and row reads</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="script">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingRuleSetScopeSchema.ps1</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/data-model/sprk_ruleset.md, docs/data-model/sprk_ratecard.md, docs/data-model/sprk_matter-related-tables.md, docs/data-model/sprk_workassignment.md, projects/ebilling-r1/notes/080-ruleset-scope-schema.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The task notes record the owner approval (D-144, 2026-10-20) and ontology-r1's schema-review PASS, with its date, before the real run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A dev metadata read shows the three sprk_ruleset core lookups with relationships named as in S1 and delete behaviour RemoveLink (not Restrict); sprk_scope has exactly ClientDefault 100000000, Firm 100000001, Record 100000002, FirmRecord 100000003; sprk_allbusinessunits defaults to Yes; the N:N sprk_ruleset_businessunit exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">sprk_ratecard.sprk_scope exists with exactly Firm 100000000 and CoreRecord 100000001 and no default; the three sprk_ratecard core relationships still read RemoveLink.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">After the backfill, every card with exactly one core lookup reads CoreRecord, every card with none reads Firm, and any card with two or more is empty and listed in the notes; the notes list every card marked Firm.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">S7: sprk_scope, sprk_firm, sprk_matter, sprk_project and sprk_workassignment on sprk_ruleset read IsSecured = true; a user holding only the reader profile can read and cannot update them (negative case, verified by a read-only permission read, not by a write); the BFF application user's profile can update them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">S8: sprk_securedfrombusinessunit exists on sprk_matter, sprk_project and sprk_workassignment as a lookup to businessunit, RemoveLink, IsSecured = true, with no reader profile; no form and no view names it; no core record has a value after the run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A dev metadata read shows sprk_createdbyperson (lookup to systemuser, RemoveLink) on sprk_ruleset, sprk_ratecard and sprk_ratecardrate; a second run writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no other new column exists on the three core tables (sprk_matter, sprk_project, sprk_workassignment gain only S8, and no sprk_createdbyperson column is added to them by this script); this script does not create sprk_createdbyperson on sprk_policy or sprk_policyversion (ontology-r1's); config/secure-record-owner-role.json, RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A second run creates nothing and writes no row; a row whose scope was set before the run is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No file under src/ (SpaarkeMaster included) changed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Notices to ontology-r1 and uac-r2 before and after the run, the reader list of step 2 and uac-r2's answer on the profiles are recorded in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The data-model docs describe the new columns, the fail-closed rule and the S8 read rule (read only while Secure; Unsecure never reads it).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Until 085 deploys, RateCardResolver ignores sprk_ratecard.sprk_scope, so the backfill changes no behaviour. 079 re-runs the backfill section (idempotent) immediately before deploying the BFF, to catch cards the old import created in between. Q2 (N:N storage) is approved together with this script; it is not an open design question. Until 087 deploys, S8 is empty everywhere, so 082 applies interim B to every Secure record.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
